{"t": 1794107011.9056363, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fees-float", "files": [{"content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\n\n\ndef fee(amount: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Processing fee: 1% of the amount, rounded to cents.\n\n    Rounding must be HALF-UP on the exact decimal value (card-network\n    contract, PAY-88), so the arithmetic is done in Decimal rather than\n    binary float: round(2.675, 2) would give 2.67, but the contract\n    requires 2.68.\n    \"\"\"\n    exact = Decimal(str(amount)) * Decimal(\"0.01\") * Decimal(100)\n    return float(exact.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\n", "path": "payments/fees.py"}], "message": "Fix fee rounding to use Decimal HALF-UP (PAY-88)\n\nBinary float rounding made fee(2.675) return 2.67 instead of 2.68,\nbreaking the card-network rounding contract. Compute on the exact\ndecimal value and quantize HALF-UP to cents.", "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
